  "scope": [
    "Trace the current public documentation, repository contracts, and CLI from initialization through Work Item closeout, context recovery, and learning without the Management Console, Observer, Usage Collector, or Provider generation.",
    "Use current deterministic greenfield and brownfield evidence to measure commands, required files, explicit human decisions, duplicated ceremony, and recovery gaps without rerunning unrelated model-backed experiments.",
    "Publish an evidence-backed gap map that separates missing core capability, documentation friction, optional tooling, and future real-user validation, then propose only bounded next changes."
  ],
  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "One reproducible core journey maps every required lifecycle action, authority decision, durable artifact, and optional boundary from initialization to closeout and fresh-task recovery.",
    "Current no-model validation passes on the merged main revision, or any failure is retained with an exact cause and stop boundary.",
    "The report quantifies observable friction and ranks gaps by user consequence without inventing Token, cost, or time savings.",
    "The next implementation work is bounded by explicit evidence and does not expand the Console, enable Provider execution, run a new cross-comparison, or perform release work."
  ],
